rules\n  * Image: checkout validation block by zipcode match\n\n  * Se kampagnevideoen for RulePilot – Checkout Rules\n  * Image: main dashboard page for rulepilot\n  * Image: create rule page to setup custom rules\n  * Image: checkout validation block by zipcode match\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRulepilot | Devpost (https://devpost.com/software/rulepilot)\nciteturn6202search8 [wordlim: 200] Published: 4 months ago; Crawled: 2 weeks ago; Rule Studio lets mods create, edit, disable, import, export, simulate, and AI-draft rules, with clear separation between rule conditions and the actions RulePilot should take. ... Divyesh Thirukonda started this project — May 22, 2026 01:17 AM EDT\n\n# Rulepilot\n\nRulepilot is a mod tool for subreddits with rules that are too nuanced for AutoModerator alone.\n\n  * Example list of rules a sub might have\n\n  * Each rule has some background context. This one is to prevent cheaters.\n\n  * Mods can add a set of conditions, including positive/negative examples, regex, semantics (AI-interpreted) and many more available.\n\n  * Mods can choose what to do with the rule-breaking posts\n\n  * Violations show up in the mod queue\n\n# About the Project\n\n## Inspiration\n\nI opened Reddit and a few posts on r/csmajors had shown up. One of them was clearly a spam post trying to market his own app, which was against the rules of the subreddit. Granted it was taken down by a moderator, but not before 3 people had commented \"spam\" on it. If only AutoModerator could have caught it.\n\nModerators often deal with rules that are easy for humans to understand but hard to express with regex. In r/csMajors, for example, posts about Amazon get routed to a megathread, posts about live online assessments are not allowed, and posts about programming humor should be sent to a different subreddit. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nPayment rules &amp; restricitons (https://community.shopify.com/t/payment-rules-restricitons/574993)\nciteturn6202search9 [wordlim: 200] Published: 11 months ago; Crawled: 3 months ago; Silax November 11, 2025, 7:39am 1 ... You should be able to use this app RulePilot to setup the exact rule to hide your payment method.\n\n# Payment rules & restricitons\n\nStore Design\n\ndesign, customizations\n\nSilax November 11, 2025, 7:39am 1\n\nI’d like to restrict or “hide” certain as a payment method depending on the user’s country.\n\nScreenshot 2025-11-11 at 1.44.58 PM784×888 42.7 KB\n\nScreenshot 2025-11-11 at 1.46.09 PM804×920 47.1 KB\n\nI tried using the “Kings checkout rule” app. but its not working. developer is no help.\n\nI am able to disable Paypal, but can’t seem to disable Stripe\n\nHope someone here has a solution to this.\n\nDitalTek November 11, 2025, 9:35am 2\n\n@Silax\n\nWhere are you want hide payment method? If on checkout page the Payment Method you cannot custom directly by code or setting as you want, If the app does not support you can try other app.\n\nDarian1 November 11, 2025, 5:09pm 3\n\nYou can do this with checkout plus. Using the payment customizations feature there is an option to hide shipping options based on the selected country. Here is an example screenshot:\n\nScreenshot 2025-11-11 at 8.43.02 AM2250×1226 208 KB\n\nThis also should work for the Stripe option Image: :+1:\n\nAlex_Tan2 December 31, 2025, 11:00am 4\n\nHey! You can use a checkout customization app using Shopify Functions.\nIt can hide specific payment methods (including Stripe/PayPal) based on country/region, and you can also add checkout validation rules if needed.\nYou should be able to use this app RulePilot to setup the exact rule to hide your payment method.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRulePilot: Агент на основе LLM для генерации правил безопасности | alphaXiv (https://www.alphaxiv.org/ru/overview/2511.12224)\nciteturn6202search10 [wordlim: 200] Published: 11 months ago; Crawled: 2 months ago; # RulePilot: An LLM-Powered Agent for Security Rule Generation ... November 15, 2025\n\n# RulePilot: An LLM-Powered Agent for Security Rule Generation\n\nRulePilot: Агент на основе LLM для генерации правил безопасности\n\nNovember 15, 2025\n\nCopy Markdown\n\nHongtai Wang, Ming Xu, Yanpei Guo, Weili Han, Hoon Wei Lim, Jin Song Dong\n\n### Резюме\n\nАгент RulePilot, работающий на базе больших языковых моделей (LLM), автоматизирует генерацию сложных правил обнаружения в системах управления информацией и событиями безопасности (SIEM) и облегчает их конвертацию между платформами, используя структурированное мышление и обратную связь в реальном времени. Он достигает более высокой точности и возможностей обнаружения в реальных условиях по сравнению с автономными большими языковыми моделями, демонстрируя эффективную генерацию исполняемых правил в реальных средах SIEM.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRac2 GTPase Activation Is Necessary for Development of p190-BCR-ABL-Induced B-Cell Acute Lymphoblastic Leukemia | Blood | American Society of Hematology (https://ashpublications.org/blood/article/112/11/3790/61317/Rac2-GTPase-Activation-Is-Necessary-for)\nciteturn6202search11 [wordlim: 200] Published: 17.9 years ago; Crawled: 2 weeks ago; Oncogenes and Tumor Suppressors| November 16, 2008 ... In the murine model of B-ALL, loss of Rac2, but not Rac3, prolonged survival and impaired leukemia development.\nIn the murine model of B-ALL, loss of Rac2, but not Rac3, prolonged survival and impaired leukemia development. Like in Ba/F3 cells, primary B-CFU and outgrowth in Witte-Whitlock assays of leukemic primary cells from mice was severely decreased by the addition of NSC23766 to the culture. Although Vav was activated by both p190- and p210-BCR-ABL, since NSC23766 does not block the activation by Vav1, we hypothesized that other GEFs were involved. Indeed, the loss of Vav1 or even combined loss of Vav1 and Vav2 did not impair BCR-ABL-mediated lymphoid leukemogenesis in vivo. Vav3, another member in the Vav family which uses a different mechanism of activation of Rac GTPases was a likely candidate. In fact, loss of Vav3 alone was able to significantly prolong the survival and attenuate development of p190 BCR-ABL-driven B-ALL. In conclusion, the results of this study indicate that Rac activation is necessary for the development of B-ALL induced by p190-BCR-ABL in vitro and in vivo, and validate a new signaling pathway as a therapeutic target for BCR-ABL-induced B-ALL.\n\nTopics: burkitt's lymphoma, guanosine triphosphate phosphohydrolases, leukemia, b-cell, acute, bcr-abl tyrosine kinase, doxorubicin/etoposide/vincristine protocol, tyrosine kinase inhibitors, rho gtp-binding proteins, flow cytometry, guanine nucleotide exchange factors, leukemia\n\nDisclosures: No relevant conflicts of interest to declare.\n\n## Author notes\n\nCorresponding author\n\n2008, The American Society of Hematology\n\n2008\n\nVolume 112, Issue 11\n\nNovember 16 2008--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nToward LLM-Driven Rule Generation for Enforcement Systems: (https://people.cs.vt.edu/djwillia/papers/agenticos26-vibewaf.pdf)\nciteturn6202search18 [wordlim: 200] Published: 5 months ago; Models for Access Control Policy Synthesis and Summarization. arXiv preprint ... RulePilot: An LLM-Powered Agent for Security Rule ... Detection: Architecture, Opportunities and Case Study. arXiv preprint (2025). ... Code Analysis, Malware Analysis, Reverse Engineering. arXiv preprint (2025).\n"
